Keep one main training dataset in memory, not too many duplicates.

Use efficient formats and rolling windows.

Archive older feature matrices instead of keeping everything hot in RAM.

Prefer one well-designed TFT over many oversized variants.

Phase 15: Production governance
A professional TFT system for gold trading must include governance rules before it goes live:

promote only models that beat baseline and existing ensemble in walk-forward tests

quarantine models whose interval calibration breaks

retrain on schedule, but not so frequently that you chase noise

keep champion vs challenger versions

maintain rollback to the last stable model

document feature list, horizon definition, quantiles, training period, and live performance drift

Final blueprint
Your professional TFT stack for gold trading should be:

Market data + macro data + HMM outputs + Wavelet outputs -> TFT multi-horizon quantile forecast -> ensemble decision layer -> risk-adjusted execution engine.

The biggest professional mistake would be to use TFT as a flashy standalone predictor. The best professional use is to make TFT the forecast-confidence module inside your existing gold architecture, where it improves timing, filtering, and dynamic position sizing rather than replacing the rest of the stack.